# Accuracy reports

Ground truth is NGSPICE using the identical BSIM-CMG LEVEL=72 OSDI model.
See [`methodology.md`](methodology.md) for gate and evidence rules.

The [root README](../../README.md) owns package release metadata. A maintenance
release does not requalify these measurements; each report names its evidence
pass. The [campaign plans](../plans/) distinguish frozen training and corrected
runtime evaluation.

## Current NN policy

DirectNet-Full LEVEL=75 is the default NN path. BSIM-AR-Full LEVEL=76 is the
autoregressive alternative. Retired LEVEL=73/74 reports are available in Git
history; [the changelog](../CHANGELOG.md#v775--repository-cleanup) records their
last revision.

## Current reports

| file | scope |
|---|---|
| [`DirectNet-L75-clean.md`](DirectNet-L75-clean.md) | latest LEVEL=75 clean qualification and gaps |
| [`BSIM-AR-L76-clean.md`](BSIM-AR-L76-clean.md) | clean LEVEL=76 qualification or explicit incomplete-matrix status |
| [`BSIM-AR-L76-simple-circuits.md`](BSIM-AR-L76-simple-circuits.md) | TSMC5 LEVEL=76 recovery; not a five-tech matrix |
| [`simple-circuits-v2-topologies.md`](simple-circuits-v2-topologies.md) | held-out topology and promotion contract |

## Clean scoreboard

<!--SCOREBOARD-->

Default status does not rewrite measured limitations. Reports require one
complete provenance-bound campaign; partial passes are never backfilled.
The builder emits clean reports only; named recipe summaries remain in their
isolated run directories. Reproduction commands live in the repository
[README](../../README.md#run-the-complete-clean-checkpoint-matrix).
